## GRADING (binding; capability decides)
- **G-1 delta (D1).** A third path, a `packages/api-contract` byte or a product byte other than the one file's = **Blocker** (STOP if security-shaped); a head blob unequal to B743's recorded blobs = **Blocker** (a different head than the gated one); a sentence unequal to the one `setPolicyTarget` answers at main, or any new customer-facing string = **Major** (it voids the "no new words" claim and the words rule); a person's name or secret = **Blocker**; non-ASCII or a skip/only = **Major**; a Jira key or work number in a new title = **Note** (B743 N3), in the squash text = **Minor** (corrected in your files); `localdomain`/local-host identity in the squash text = **Major**; a false PR-body sentence = **Minor** (replaced in `pr-body.txt`).
- **G-2 the merge result and the ticket (D2, D4).** A merge conflict, or the merge result's product bytes unequal to the head's = **Major** (class); a moved file the new test imports whose moved bytes change a helper it uses = **Major** unless the new file is still green on the merge result (then **Minor**, say why); a ticket closing condition the file does not cover = **Major**; a statement in the diff, PR body or commits that a run does not back = **Minor** (corrected), **Major** if about the refusal claim.
- **G-3 the runs (D3, D5).** A new row red or flaky on the merge result (any of 3 runs, the shuffle) = **Major, class**; the group other than main + 1 file + the new rows, or names other than lost 0 / added = new rows = **Major** unless explained; an old row red on the merge result that is green at main = **Major, class**; p1 leaving the refusing rows green = **Major** (the rows cannot fail); p2 leaving every row green = **Major**; lint, prettier or the unit step rc non-zero = **Major** (CI's node step fails); no tsc over `apps/api/test` = **Note** (B743 D1, pre-existing); p3 green everywhere = **Note**.
- **G-4 CodeQL and the cap (D6).** An open alert on the head or the merge ref = **Blocker** and STOP; NOT SCANNED = a **Condition** (never green by inference; Tuesday lands only after a clean scan); a clean scan of the head = no entry. **Always Note:** the dependabot banner; the local-host identity of the PR commits (the squash sets the author).
- **G-5 verdict (round 1 of 2).** Any Blocker or Major = `NO GO (round 1 of 2)` (fix-shapes in prose; "a second NO GO on this class goes to the product owner on a card"); Minors/Notes only = `GO WITH FOLLOW-UPS`; none above Note = `GO`. Always add ` (conditional: CodeQL NOT SCANNED)` while D6 is not "scanned and clean", and any other unrun required check.

